{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Dry-run evidence (recorded before the live run, per the plan)\n\nRead-only `propose_migrations('.', include_open=True)` against the real store, at\ncommit 64cefd6 (Gerrit change 971).\n\n**Sizing — 104 tickets would be migrated:**\n\n| status | count |\n|---|---|\n| closed | 91 |\n| idea | 10 |\n| open | 2 |\n| in_progress | 1 |\n\nThe 3 non-closed tickets are `119f-63e3-34b7-4f96` (in_progress, shy-fussy-hermitcrab),\n`55de-25ab-ca20-4c79` (open, harm-inlay-drift) and `be74-7832-03a8-48ac` (open,\nslimy-tuber-stoop). **None is actively claimed** — all three have `claimed_session=None`\nand no assignee — so no in-flight agent's work is disrupted. Their plan-review\nattestations will go stale (`stale-material`), which is the expected and unavoidable cost\nthe plan anticipates: the plan text genuinely changes.\n\n**A real defect the dry-run caught, before any write.** The first implementation was\nsensitive to section ORDER. Where `## Success Criteria` preceded `## Acceptance Criteria`,\nthe merge kept the SC heading, duplicated the criterion, duplicated the entire AC block,\nand was not idempotent. **97 of the 104 affected tickets are in exactly that order**, so a\nlive run would have corrupted the large majority of them. Fixed by rebuilding the rewrite\naround an order-agnostic `_splice(description, edits)` helper instead of hand-assembled\nslice arithmetic, and pinned by four new held-out cases (SC-before-AC merge, no-duplicate-\nheading across both orders, headings-on-their-own-line, idempotency for SC-first).\n\n**Post-fix invariants across all 104 proposed rewrites:**\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| `## Success Criteria` survives | 0 |\n| AC heading duplicated by migration | 0 |\n| non-idempotent | 0 |\n| fails the AC floor (`_count_ac_items < 1`) | 0 |\n| suspicious length growth (>1.6x) | 0 |\n\nThree tickets (`4702-a55c-7aeb-445a`, `8e17-8aca-998f-4f62`, `b02d-10bc-07ee-49e7`) carry\ntwo `## Acceptance Criteria` headings *both before and after* migration — pre-existing in\nthe source tickets, faithfully preserved rather than introduced.\n\nFull oracle: 22/22 green (2 happy-path + 20 held-out). Mutation-tested: no-op checkbox\nconversion, `###`-terminates-block, and never-merge each turn the relevant held-out cases\nRED. `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the script's own ruff pass clean; 179 LOC.\n\nOperator approved the FULL 104-ticket run (including the 3 non-closed tickets) rather than\na closed-only subset. Live run will follow once change 971 is LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785005814982007001,"uuid":"9ac63084-dad0-4a16-97df-9496d72fde5b"}